Subject: [PATCH 1/6] docs: recompute the Pure MPC row from the artifacts and
 lift the void mark

Now that the lower window's T0-T5 artifacts are on the branch, the four
horizon rows were recomputed here from the per-episode JSON rather than
quoted. The h35 figures the earlier handoff asserted without artifacts
reproduce: 9/12, 88.5 s and 167.2 N s against the 9/12, 88.4 s and 167.2 N s
it claimed, so the unreproduced mark on that row is lifted. The two audit
figure sets remain void; their scripts are still absent.

Two things the recomputation adds that the summaries did not. The worst
per-step cost at every horizon is step zero, with the runner-up between 69
and 129 ms, so the max column describes a cold start a flight system pays
once rather than a recurring tail. And what actually separates h35 from h50
is not the p95 (0.77x against 1.14x, which reads as a near miss) but the
number of steps over the control period: 2 of 300 against 269 of 300.

h20 and h50 carry no fuel figure because their completed episodes come from
the earlier batch, whose records have no force-impulse field. Recorded as
missing rather than filled from a different horizon.

