Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix: report the gated truth margin, not the raw per-key
 minima

The evaluation path recorded the minimum of each raw task margin field over
every control step, whether or not that constraint was live. A chaser 17 m
out and off the approach axis carries a corridor margin near -19 m, which is
not a violation because the corridor is not a constraint out there, so a
completing zero-violation episode was reported at -3.394 m and the column
mixed metres, radians and m/s besides. The table built from it would have
described the safest rows as the worst.

Each episode now also records the minimum of normalized_precapture_truth_margins,
which gates inactive rows to a large positive value and divides every active
row by its own limit, and the main_table block carries the worst of those over
all episodes. This is the same quantity the horizon rows already report, so
the coupled row and the Pure MPC row become comparable.

Verified on the two-episode control: the completing episode reads +0.146 where
the raw column read -3.394, and the episode that failed on field of view reads
-0.0007, matching its recorded 49.92 deg against the 50 deg limit.

