The file still described the single_phase task, the Waypoint and the A1-A3
perception line as current, so a session starting cold reoriented itself
around work that has been closed for a week. It now leads with the
precapture task, the frozen coupling interface, the verified Pure MPC row
and what T7 did and did not establish, and keeps the old line only for the
three lessons that still bind -- the pinned entropy temperature, hovering as
a real attractor, and re-evaluation flipping published numbers.

The traps section is rebuilt around the ones that have actually cost time
here: ungated raw margins, the predicted margin not being free or a truth
margin, stale slack on fallback steps, the wrapper's transparency condition,
silent observation mismatches on checkpoint load, and the two compute
reporting pitfalls. It also records which figures are void for want of any
artifact.

