Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 04:44:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] docs: verify the headline interface claim as a single
 factor

The claim that the action parametrisation is what made the coupling
learnable was being quoted rather than checked. Comparing the manifests
field by field, the old radial_local batch and the new arrival_condition
batch share the observation (31D), the horizon, the decision period, the
discount, the learning rate, batch size, entropy coefficient, tau,
learning-starts, the network and the frozen task. The parametrisation is the
only difference, so this is a single-factor comparison rather than a change
of setup.

Recomputed at the common budget of 25,697 decisions, which is where the old
batch stopped: radial_local completes 0 of 1308 episodes across three seeds,
while arrival_condition reaches 55 of 285 on its best seed. The earlier
observation factor -- adding target attitude phase and remaining time --
changed nothing on the old parametrisation, so information was not the
binding constraint and expression was.

Records what the comparison does not support: both batches still lose half
their seeds, the 75% figure is a training-episode rate under exploration and
not an evaluation score, and both batches are below the three-seed rule.

